{
  "_doc": "The one list behind no-retro-rerender.py (PreToolUse) and no-retro-rerender-stop.py (Stop). Already-shipped work keeps the style it shipped with. Sending an existing asset back through its generator so it matches a newer style is blocked, on every surface and for every asset type: images, covers, cards, films, tiles, decks, logos, pages and copy.",
  "_code_doc": "Code that sends an already-shipped asset back to a generator. The tell is a backfill: a sweep over historical rows that clears the asset field, a loop that re-renders every existing asset, or a gate that refuses a reused asset. Writing a new asset for a row that never had one is not this and must never match.",
